      "raw_text": "To solve this problem, we will break it down into logical steps:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of flowers planted.**\nRyan plants 2 flowers every day for 15 days.\n$$ \\text{Total planted} = \\text{Flowers per day} \\times \\text{Number of days} $$\n$$ \\text{Total planted} = 2 \\times 15 = 30 \\text{ flowers} $$\n\n**Step 2: Account for the flowers that did not grow.**\nThe problem states that out of the planted flowers, 5 did not grow. We need to subtract these from the total planted amount to find the number of flowers that actually grew.\n$$ \\text{Flowers grown} = \\text{Total planted} - \\text{Flowers that did not grow} $$\n$$ \\text{Flowers grown} = 30 - 5 = 25 \\text{ flowers} $$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nAfter 15 days, Ryan has 25 flowers in his garden.\n\n#### 25<|im_end|>",
      "answer_text": "To solve this problem, we will break it down into logical steps:\n\n**Step 1: Calculate the total number of flowers planted.**\nRyan plants 2 flowers every day for 15 days.\n$$ \\text{Total planted} = \\text{Flowers per day} \\times \\text{Number of days} $$\n$$ \\text{Total planted} = 2 \\times 15 = 30 \\text{ flowers} $$\n\n**Step 2: Account for the flowers that did not grow.**\nThe problem states that out of the planted flowers, 5 did not grow. We need to subtract these from the total planted amount to find the number of flowers that actually grew.\n$$ \\text{Flowers grown} = \\text{Total planted} - \\text{Flowers that did not grow} $$\n$$ \\text{Flowers grown} = 30 - 5 = 25 \\text{ flowers} $$\n\n**Conclusion:**\nAfter 15 days, Ryan has 25 flowers in his garden.\n\n#### 25",
